#X obj 688 11 env.ar~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 326 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A simple AR (Attack / Release) envelope generator with
two stages: attack (rise from 0 to 1) and release (fall back to 0).
Unlike [env.adsr~] \, it has no decay or sustain stage \, so it is
triggered by a bang or a gate and immediately starts fading out after
the attack is complete. The envelope multiplies the incoming audio
signal by its current value.;
#X text 240 199 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 224 • Percussive sounds — shaping the amplitude of a short
hit or click \, where the sound should fade out naturally after the
attack without holding a sustain level.;
#X text 250 279 • Plucked string emulation — reproducing the natural
decay of a plucked string or a struck bell \, where there is no sustain
phase.;
#X text 250 334 • Modulation envelopes — modulating filter cutoff \,
pitch \, or pan with a short attack-release shape to add accents or
movement to a parameter.;
